                                                "sense_id": "3c9b834e-5d47-3d5f-b8e2-a99127188802",
                                                "text": "The musician on the left is playing the zampogna, a bagpipe with two chanters and two drones. The zampogna is thought to be the bag-provided descendant of the ancient mouth-blown divergent pipes of the Romans, known as the tibia."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
